6. INSTRUMENT FAULT FOUND AND FIXED DURING THIS CASE
-----------------------------------------------------
First cut of `tools/arpleg.py` passed `-p` (non-promiscuous) to tcpdump.  A routed frame leaves
the DUT carrying the destination MAC of the NEXT HOP -- here the static entry's fake
00:11:22:33:44:99 -- which is not the capturing NIC's own MAC, so the kernel dropped every one of
them before tcpdump saw it.

  leg L1-static-on  (with -p):  eth4 capture held 0 forwarded frames
  leg L1b-static-on (without):  eth4 capture held 5 of 5, dst MAC 00:11:22:33:44:99

Identical DUT configuration both times.  With `-p` the leg reads exactly like "the DUT forwarded
nothing", i.e. indistinguishable from the feature being broken.

Fixed in `tools/arpleg.py`: captures are PROMISCUOUS by default, `--no-promisc` is opt-in, and
the reason is written into the function's docstring so it cannot be re-introduced.  Legs L0 and
L1 were both re-run after the fix (L0b, L1b) so the baseline and the measurement share one
instrument.  The pre-fix legs are retained at /tmp/ck1747/T33248/L0-off-*.pcap and
L1-static-on-*.pcap as the record of the fault.

This is exactly the failure mode the "two independent counters" rule exists for, and it is the
reason no verdict in this group rests on a single counter.


